📌 Title Idea
Architecting Resilient Data Pipelines with Self-Hosted Orchestration & Automated SQL Upserts

📝 Abstract
Modern tech teams waste hundreds of hours manually processing unstructured data, running ad‑hoc scripts, and fixing fragile cloud API integrations that break on network drops. By building persistent, self‑hosted automation pipelines, teams can streamline complex data ingestion while cutting cloud service costs.

This guide demonstrates how to build and host a resilient automation workflow that ingests external data (webhooks, PDFs, or APIs), validates payloads, and safely updates a central PostgreSQL database using persistent retry queues.

🚀 Key Takeaways
Self-Hosted Architecture  
Deploy an open‑source orchestration engine (like n8n or lightweight Docker container workers) to maintain total data privacy.

Queue-Based Reliability  
Implement exponential backoff retries so data is never lost during API or network downtime.

Database Integration  
Structure secure SQL upsert queries to process large datasets safely and efficiently.

